{"id":"3-methyl-pcpy","name":"3-methyl-PCPy","form":"capsule","status":"Reference","source":"Wikidata","wikidata":"Q75614687","aliases":"","category":"Dissociative","chemicalClass":"Arylcyclohexylamines","groups":[],"atc":[],"summary":"3-Methyl-PCPy (3-Me-PCPy) is an arylcyclohexylamine derivative with an unusual spectrum of pharmacological effects, acting as both a potent NMDA antagonist and also a triple reuptake inhibitor which inhibits reuptake of all three monoamine neurotransmitters serotonin, dopamine and noradrenaline. It also acts as a high affinity sigma receptor ligand, selective for the σ2 subtype.","summarySources":"Wikipedia","doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Smoked","source":"FreeODwiki","unit":"mg","threshold":"2 mg","light":"5–10 mg","common":"10–20 mg","strong":"20–25 mg","heavy":"25 mg+","commonEstimate":15,"band":{"low":10,"high":20},"domain":[1.6,44],"segments":{"light":[5,10],"common":[10,20],"strong":[20,25],"heavy":[25,42.24]}},{"roa":"Oral","source":"FreeODwiki","unit":"mg","threshold":"5 mg","light":"5–10 mg","common":"10–20 mg","strong":"20–30 mg","heavy":"30 mg+","commonEstimate":15,"band":{"low":10,"high":20},"domain":[4,44],"segments":{"light":[5,10],"common":[10,20],"strong":[20,30],"heavy":[30,42.24]}},{"roa":"Insufflated","source":"FreeODwiki","unit":"mg","threshold":"5 mg","light":"5–10 mg","common":"10–20 mg","strong":"20–25 mg","heavy":"25 mg+","commonEstimate":15,"band":{"low":10,"high":20},"domain":[4,44],"segments":{"light":[5,10],"common":[10,20],"strong":[20,25],"heavy":[25,42.24]}}],"durationRows":[{"roa":"Smoked","onset":"—","comeup":"—","peak":"—","offset":"—","afterEffects":"—","total":"0.75–2 h"},{"roa":"Oral","onset":"30–90 min","comeup":"0.75–2 h","peak":"2–3 h","offset":"1–2 h","afterEffects":"4–48 h","total":"4–8 h"},{"roa":"Insufflated","onset":"5–30 min","comeup":"45–90 min","peak":"1.5–2 h","offset":"45–60 min","afterEffects":"4–48 h","total":"3–5 h"}],"subjectiveEffects":[],"combinations":[],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3-Methyl-PCPy"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on 3-methyl-PCPy","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q75614687"},{"title":"PubChem","description":"Chemistry, safety and literature","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/137332188"},{"title":"FreeODwiki","description":"Doses and timings, in Chinese","url":"https://freeodwiki.org/%E8%8D%AF%E7%89%A9/3-Me-PCPy.html"}],"formula":"C17H25N","molarMass":243.4,"doseMaxTick":50,"durationSources":"FreeODwiki","advisory":"Heavy doses can bring on psychosis and mania.","advisorySource":"FreeODwiki","pharmacology":{"text":"In in vitro binding assays, 3-Me-PCPy displays high affinities across monoamine reuptake transporters alongside the NMDA receptor complex. Unusually for an arylcyclohexylamine dissociative, its affinity for the serotonin transporter (SERT) is approximately ten-fold higher than its affinity for the NMDA receptor pore.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"3-Methyl-PCPy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/3-Methyl-PCPy#Pharmacology"}}